    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Three Kingdoms\"\nauthor: \"DK\"\ndate: \"2026-10-21\"\ncategories: [dynasties]\n---\n\n\n## 서울의 궁궐 — Three Royal Palaces\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(leaflet)\n\npalaces <- data.frame(\n  name = c(\"덕수궁 (Deoksugung Palace)\",\n           \"창덕궁 (Changdeokgung Palace)\",\n           \"경복궁 (Gyeongbokgung Palace)\"),\n  lat = c(37.56500, 37.57944, 37.57960),\n  lng = c(126.97652, 126.99278, 126.97700),\n  address = c(\"99 Sejong-daero, Jung-gu\",\n              \"99 Yulgok-ro, Jongno-gu\",\n              \"161 Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu\")\n)\n\nleaflet(palaces) |>\n  addProviderTiles(\"OpenStreetMap\") |>\n  addMarkers(\n    lng = ~lng,\n    lat = ~lat,\n    label = ~name,\n    popup = ~paste0(\n      \"<strong>\", name, \"</strong><br>\",\n      address, \"<br>\",\n      \"<a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=\",\n      lat, \",\", lng,\n      \"' target='_blank'>Open in Google Maps</a>\"\n    )\n  ) |>\n  fitBounds(\n    lng1 = min(palaces$lng) - 0.005,\n    lat1 = min(palaces$lat) - 0.005,\n    lng2 = max(palaces$lng) + 0.005,\n    lat2 = max(palaces$lat) + 0.005\n  )\n```\n\n::: {#fig-seoul-palaces .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"leaflet html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-6e526c8d95da31fb593c\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-6e526c8d95da31fb593c\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}}},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"OpenStreetMap\",null,null,{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addMarkers\",\"args\":[[37.565,37.57944,37.5796],[126.97652,126.99278,126.977],null,null,null,{\"interactive\":true,\"draggable\":false,\"keyboard\":true,\"title\":\"\",\"alt\":\"\",\"zIndexOffset\":0,\"opacity\":1,\"riseOnHover\":false,\"riseOffset\":250},[\"<strong>덕수궁 (Deoksugung Palace)<\\/strong><br>99 Sejong-daero, Jung-gu<br><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=37.565,126.97652' target='_blank'>Open in Google Maps<\\/a>\",\"<strong>창덕궁 (Changdeokgung Palace)<\\/strong><br>99 Yulgok-ro, Jongno-gu<br><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=37.57944,126.99278' target='_blank'>Open in Google Maps<\\/a>\",\"<strong>경복궁 (Gyeongbokgung Palace)<\\/strong><br>161 Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu<br><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=37.5796,126.977' target='_blank'>Open in Google Maps<\\/a>\"],null,null,null,[\"덕수궁 (Deoksugung Palace)\",\"창덕궁 (Changdeokgung Palace)\",\"경복궁 (Gyeongbokgung Palace)\"],{\"interactive\":false,\"permanent\":false,\"direction\":\"auto\",\"opacity\":1,\"offset\":[0,0],\"textsize\":\"10px\",\"textOnly\":false,\"className\":\"\",\"sticky\":true},null]}],\"limits\":{\"lat\":[37.565,37.5796],\"lng\":[126.97652,126.99278]},\"fitBounds\":[37.56,126.97152,37.5846,126.99778,[]]},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe three palaces form a compact triangle in central Seoul. Using approximate palace locations and walking-route estimates, the shortest side is between Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung, while Deoksugung sits farther southwest. \n\nApproximate distances\nPair of palaces\tStraight-line distance\tApprox. walking distance\n- 경복궁 ↔ 창덕궁\t1.4 km\t1.5–2 km\n- 경복궁 ↔ 덕수궁\t1.7 km\t2–2.3 km\n- 창덕궁 ↔ 덕수궁\t2.4 km\t2.5–3 km\n",
